<title>UK: Sainsbury up as Capel raises to &quot;hold&quot;.</title>
<headline>Sainsbury up as Capel raises to &quot;hold&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in J. Sainsbury Plc rose on Monday as analysts at HSBC James Capel raised the supermarket stock to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;sell,&quot; market sources said. The stock was up 4-1/2p at 366 by 1136 GMT, extending a rebound since it fell to a low of 341p on November 14 -- its lowest since January 1992.</p>
<p>Analyst Frank Davidson at Capel declined comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
